    "['ip nat inside source static network [parameter1] [parameter2] [parameter3]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set security nat static rule-set NAT-RULE from zone untrust', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set security nat static rule-set NAT-RULE from zone untrust', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco NAT static network mapping command:\\n\\n##\\nset security nat static rule-set NAT-RULE from zone untrust\\nset security nat static rule-set NAT-RULE rule NETWORK-NAT match destination-address 11.11.11.0/24\\nset security nat static rule-set NAT-RULE rule NETWORK-NAT then static-nat prefix 10.0.0.0/24\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. Juniper uses a different NAT structure with rule-sets and explicit zone associations\\n2. The translation maps the entire /24 network (10.0.0.0) to the external /24 network (11.11.11.0)\\n3. \"untrust\" is used as the destination zone, which should be adjusted based on your actual zone naming\\n4. You may need to configure appropriate security policies to allow this traffic', 'trans_template': 'set security nat static rule-set NAT-RULE from zone untrust'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set security nat static rule-set NAT-RULE rule NETWORK-NAT match destination-address 11.11.11.0/24', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set security nat static rule-set NAT-RULE rule NETWORK-NAT match destination-address 11.11.11.0/24', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco NAT static network mapping command:\\n\\n##\\nset security nat static rule-set NAT-RULE from zone untrust\\nset security nat static rule-set NAT-RULE rule NETWORK-NAT match destination-address 11.11.11.0/24\\nset security nat static rule-set NAT-RULE rule NETWORK-NAT then static-nat prefix 10.0.0.0/24\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. Juniper uses a different NAT structure with rule-sets and explicit zone associations\\n2. The translation maps the entire /24 network (10.0.0.0) to the external /24 network (11.11.11.0