    "['access-list [parameter1] [parameter2] [parameter3] [parameter4] [parameter5] [parameter6]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set firewall family inet filter ACL-100 term 10 from source-address 10.0.0.0/24', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set firewall family inet filter ACL-100 term 10 from source-address 10.0.0.0/24', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco ACL command:\\n\\n##\\nset firewall family inet filter ACL-100 term 10 from source-address 10.0.0.0/24\\nset firewall family inet filter ACL-100 term 10 then accept\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- Juniper uses hierarchical configuration with `set` commands\\n- `firewall family inet` specifies IPv4 filtering\\n- The filter is named `ACL-100` (matching Cisco\\'s ACL 100)\\n- `term 10` is a term/entry in the filter (equivalent to ACL line)\\n- `source-address 10.0.0.0/24` matches the Cisco wildcard mask 0.0.0.255\\n- `then accept` is the permit action\\n- The \"any\" destination is implied by not specifying a destination match', 'trans_template': 'set firewall family inet filter ACL-100 term 10 from source-address 10.0.0.0/24'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set firewall family inet filter ACL-100 term 10 then accept', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set firewall family inet filter ACL-100 term 10 then accept', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco ACL command:\\n\\n##\\nset firewall family inet filter ACL-100 term 10 from source-address 10.0.0.0/24\\nset firewall family inet filter ACL-100 term 10 then accept\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- Juniper uses hierarchical configuration with `set` commands\\n- `firewall family inet` specifies IPv4 filtering\\n- The filter is named `ACL-100` (matching Cisco\\'s ACL 100)\\n- `term 10` is a term/entry in the filter (equivalent to ACL line)\\n- `source-address 10.0.0.0/24` matches the Cisco wildcard mask 0.0.0.255\\n- `then accept` is the permit action\\n- The \"any\" destination is implied by not specifying a destination match', 'trans_template': 'set firewall family inet filter ACL-100 term 10 then accept'}]]": 1,
    "['class-map match-all [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'class NAT-CLASS {', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'class NAT-CLASS {', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Juniper configuration command for the Cisco `class-map` statement:\\n\\n##\\nclass NAT-CLASS {\\n    match-all;\\n}\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Juniper, `class` is used instead of `class-map`\\n- The `match-all` behavior is preserved (meaning all conditions must match)\\n- The syntax follows Juniper's hierarchical structure with curly braces\\n- The name `NAT-CLASS` is preserved as the class identifier\\n\\nThis would be part of Juniper's class-of-service (CoS) configuration hierarchy, similar to how Cisco uses class maps for traffic classification.\", 'trans_template': 'class NAT-CLASS {'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'match-all;', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'match-all;', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Juniper configuration command for the Cisco `class-map` statement:\\n\\n##\\nclass NAT-CLASS {\\n    match-all;\\n}\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Juniper, `class` is used instead of `class-map`\\n- The `match-all` behavior is preserved (meaning all conditions must match)\\n- The syntax follows Juniper's hierarchical structure with curly braces\\n- The name `NAT-CLASS` is preserved as the class identifier\\n\\nThis would be part of Juniper's class-of-service (CoS) configuration hierarchy, similar to how Cisco uses class maps for traffic classification.\", 'trans_template': 'match-all;'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': '}', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'interfaces [parameter2]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Juniper configuration command for the Cisco `class-map` statement:\\n\\n##\\nclass NAT-CLASS {\\n    match-all;\\n}\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Juniper, `class` is used instead of `class-map`\\n- The `match-all` behavior is preserved (meaning all conditions must match)\\n- The syntax foll